    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Title">Tool approval</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Description">Choose when tool calls need confirmation and manage permanently allowed entries.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Balanced.Title">Balanced · Recommended</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Balanced.Description">Run read-only tools automatically; confirm writes, deletes, and terminal commands.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Strict.Title">Strict</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Strict.Description">Confirm every tool call.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Automatic.Title">Automatic</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Automatic.Description">Let the automatic approval model evaluate calls not handled by static rules.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Off.Title">Approval off</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.Off.Description">Run every tool automatically in fully trusted environments.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.AutoAllowedHint">These tools are permanently allowed. You can revoke them at any time.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.TerminalHint">Allowlisted terminal commands do not ask for repeated confirmation.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Approval.JevShadowHint">When an approval prompt appears, the call (tool name, command line, file paths, URLs without query strings) and your last two messages are sent through OpenRouter to TypeSafe Jev in the background; the scores are logged next to your decision to judge whether Jev could pre-screen prompts. File contents and task instructions are sent as lengths only, and likely secrets are masked. It never changes an approval result and needs an OpenRouter connection with an API key.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.Title">Execution &amp; concurrency</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.Description">Configure execution limits for the main conversation and for parallel sub-agents: concurrency, tool rounds, and timeouts.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.Conversation.Title">Main conversation execution</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.Conversation.MaxParallel">Global primary-chat concurrency</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.Conversation.MaxToolRounds">Maximum tool rounds per reply</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.Conversation.MaxToolRoundsHint">Upper bound on model round-trips within a single reply. Once it runs out the reply stops mid-task and you have to say “continue” to resume. Raise it when running long multi-step skills.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.SubAgent.Title">Sub-agents</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.SubAgent.Enabled">Enable sub-agents</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.SubAgent.ModelHint">Choose the model under Providers &amp; model roles / Sub-agent.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.SubAgent.MaxParallel">Maximum parallel agents</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.SubAgent.MaxToolRounds">Maximum tool rounds per agent</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.ProviderRetry.Title">Provider requests</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.ProviderRetry.Description">Resend the same request when the provider cuts the reply stream off midway. A round that has already started writing answer text is never retried — resending would make the model write it all over again.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.ProviderRetry.Enabled">Retry interrupted requests automatically</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.ProviderRetry.MaxAttempts">Maximum retries</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.ProviderRetry.InitialDelay">Wait before the first retry (seconds)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.ProviderRetry.Backoff">Each further wait doubles, capped at 30 seconds each and 60 seconds per round.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Agent.SubAgent.Timeout">Timeout (seconds)</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.Title">Runtime diagnostics</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.Description">Inspect local model/context state, manage relearnable caches, and check browser runtime health.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.ContextData">Model and context data</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.ContextDataHint">Structured local diagnostics contain only revisions, counts and timestamps - no prompts, images, paths or API keys.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.MetadataCatalog">Metadata catalog</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.RefreshContextData">Refresh diagnostics</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.ClearMetadataCache">Clear metadata cache</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.ClearMetadataCacheConfirm">Clear downloaded OpenRouter metadata snapshots and return to the bundled seed?</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.MetadataCacheCleared">Downloaded metadata cache was cleared; bundled seed remains available.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.ClearFailed">Clear failed: {0}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.MetadataSummary">Revision {0} · {1:N0} models · fetched {2:g} · {3}</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.BrowserRuntime">Browser runtime</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.BrowserRuntimeHint">Automatic browser needs a local Chromium runtime. Install it here when missing.</system:String>
    <system:String x:Key="Settings.Diagnostics.BrowserAgent">Automatic browser model</system:String>

